From: NXP SDK Build <vyos@mono.si>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 22:34:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fmd: allow /dev/fm0-port-rx* opens without SDK port init

The SDK FM port driver's fm_port_probe creates sysfs devices and sets
dev_set_drvdata(), but InitFmPortDev() (which calls FM_PORT_Config +
FM_PORT_Init to populate h_Dev) is never invoked because the mainline
DPAA driver claims FMan port platform devices first. The h_Dev NULL
check in fm_open() therefore rejects all port device opens with ENODEV.

Fix: replace the h_Dev NULL check with a dev NULL check. Since
ReadFmPortDevTreeNode sets ->dev from the platform device during probe,
and dev_set_drvdata() was called, fm_port_bind(->dev) works correctly
and returns the port structure via dev_get_drvdata().

This allows dpa_app to open /dev/fm0-port-rx0 (and other port minors)
for PCD programming ioctls.

Board-verified: dpa_app v2 (3.2 MB, fmc-linked) exits 0 after
successful FMC model compilation and execution. All PCD ioctls on
/dev/fm0-pcd (0x17 load, 0x15 execute, 0x28/0x39/0x2c/0x2e) return 0.

Signed-off-by: NXP SDK Build <vyos@mono.si>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/src/wrapper/lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/src/wrapper/lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/src/wrapper/lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c
index f97c37f06..a8b5a78ec 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/src/wrapper/lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/sdk_fman/src/wrapper/lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c
@@ -4727,9 +4727,15 @@ static int fm_open(struct inode *inode, struct file *file)
         else
             return -EINVAL;
 
-        /* if trying to open port, check if it initialized */
-        if (!p_LnxWrpFmPortDev->h_Dev)
+        /* KILO-FIX: Mainline DPAA driver owns FMan port platform devices,
+         * so the SDK port driver's InitFmPortDev() is never called and
+         * h_Dev stays NULL. However, dev_set_drvdata() was called by
+         * fm_port_probe, so fm_port_bind() below works correctly.
+         * Skip the h_Dev check — the port is initialized enough for PCD ops. */
+        if (!p_LnxWrpFmPortDev->dev) {
+            pr_err("fm_open: port minor %d has no platform device\n", minor);
             return -ENODEV;
+        }
 
         p_LnxWrpFmPortDev = (t_LnxWrpFmPortDev *)fm_port_bind(p_LnxWrpFmPortDev->dev);
         file->private_data = p_LnxWrpFmPortDev;
